{title: 300 - Rock of Ages}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #300 • TOPLADY • 14.14.15}
{lyricist: Augustus M. Toplady}
{composer: Thomas Hastings}
{key: Bb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 300}
{meta: tune TOPLADY}
{meta: meter 14.14.15}
{meta: category Gospel - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]Rock of Ages, cleft for me, Let me hide [Eb]myself [F7]in [Bb]Thee;
[F]Let the [F7]water and the [Bb]blood, From Thy [F7]riven side which [Bb]flowed,
[Bb]Be of sin the double cure, Cleanse me from its [Eb]guilt [F7]and power.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Bb]Not the labor of [Eb]my [F7]hands
[Bb]Can fulfill Thy law's [Eb]demands;
[F]Could [F7]my zeal [Bb]no respite [F7]know,
[F]Could [F7]my tears [Bb]forever [F7]flow,
[Bb]All for sin could not [Eb]atone;
[Bb]Thou must save, and Thou [Eb]alone.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Bb]When my pilgrimage [Eb]I [F7]close;
[Bb]Victor o'er the last [Eb]of [F7]foes,
[F]When [F7]I soar [Bb]to worlds [F7]unknown,
[F]And [F7]behold [Bb]Thee on [F7]Thy throne,
[Bb]Rock of Ages, cleft [Eb]for [F7]me,
[Bb]Let me hide myself [Eb]in [F7]Thee.
{end_of_verse}
